Relevant tables / columns and why they matter  
• META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMTOPICS  
 – "Id": topic primary key – lets us restrict to forum topics.  
 – "FirstForumMessageId": the message that opened the topic – exactly the set we need.  

• META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGES  
 – "Id": message primary key – to join with "FirstForumMessageId".  
 – "PostUserId": author of the message – needed to know who wrote it.  

• META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES  
 – "ForumMessageId": which message was voted on.  
 – "FromUserId": voter – DISTINCT count of these equals the message‑score.  

• META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.USERS  
 – "Id": user PK (join with "PostUserId").  
 – "UserName": what we have to display.  

Typical conditions we will use  
• "FirstForumMessageId" IS NOT NULL – only topics where it is recorded.  
• JOIN FORUMMESSAGES ON FORUMMESSAGES."Id" = FORUMTOPICS."FirstForumMessageId".  
• JOIN FORUMMESSAGEVOTES … GROUP BY … COUNT(DISTINCT "FromUserId") AS "msg_score".  
• Use window‑function AVG() OVER() to compute the overall average score of all first messages.  
• Order BY "msg_score" DESC.  
• Limit 3.  
————————————————————————————————————————  
Below are ten exploratory → increasingly complex Snowflake SQL queries (all limited to 20 rows) that pave the way toward the final solution.  
All column names are double‑quoted and each query is preceded by a short comment.

```sql
-- 1. List 20 forum topics that have a recorded first message
SELECT "Id", "FirstForumMessageId"
FROM META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMTOPICS
WHERE "FirstForumMessageId" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Show the author and topic for a handful of first messages
SELECT fm."Id"            AS "MessageId",
       fm."PostUserId"    AS "AuthorId",
       ft."Id"            AS "TopicId"
FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMTOPICS     ft
JOIN   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGES   fm
  ON   fm."Id" = ft."FirstForumMessageId"
WHERE  ft."FirstForumMessageId" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Inspect votes on an arbitrary message (id hard‑coded for demo)
SELECT "Id"            AS "VoteId",
       "ForumMessageId",
       "FromUserId"
FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES
WHERE  "ForumMessageId" = 6          -- replace 6 by any valid message id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Compute message‑score (distinct voters) for 20 first messages
SELECT fm."Id"                                        AS "MessageId",
       COUNT(DISTINCT fmv."FromUserId")               AS "Msg_Score"
FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMTOPICS           ft
JOIN   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGES         fm
  ON   fm."Id" = ft."FirstForumMessageId"
LEFT JOIN META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES  fmv
  ON   fmv."ForumMessageId" = fm."Id"
WHERE  ft."FirstForumMessageId" IS NOT NULL
GROUP  BY fm."Id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Attach author usernames to the previous result
SELECT u."UserName",
       fm."Id"                         AS "MessageId",
       COUNT(DISTINCT fmv."FromUserId") AS "Msg_Score"
FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMTOPICS  ft
JOIN   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGES fm
  ON   fm."Id" = ft."FirstForumMessageId"
JOIN   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.USERS         u
  ON   u."Id" = fm."PostUserId"
LEFT JOIN META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES fmv
  ON   fmv."ForumMessageId" = fm."Id"
WHERE  ft."FirstForumMessageId" IS NOT NULL
GROUP  BY u."UserName", fm."Id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Compute the average message‑score of ALL first messages
SELECT AVG("Msg_Score") AS "Average_FirstMsg_Score"
FROM (
        SELECT fm."Id",
               COUNT(DISTINCT fmv."FromUserId") AS "Msg_Score"
        FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMTOPICS          ft
        JOIN   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGES        fm
          ON   fm."Id" = ft."FirstForumMessageId"
        LEFT JOIN META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES fmv
          ON   fmv."ForumMessageId" = fm."Id"
        WHERE  ft."FirstForumMessageId" IS NOT NULL
        GROUP  BY fm."Id"
     ) q;
```

```sql
-- 7. Bring the average into each row using a window function
SELECT fm."Id"                                  AS "MessageId",
       u."UserName",
       COUNT(DISTINCT fmv."FromUserId")         AS "Msg_Score",
       AVG(COUNT(DISTINCT fmv."FromUserId"))
         OVER ()                                AS "Avg_All_FirstMsg"
FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMTOPICS  ft
JOIN   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGES fm
  ON   fm."Id" = ft."FirstForumMessageId"
JOIN   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.USERS         u
  ON   u."Id" = fm."PostUserId"
LEFT JOIN META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES fmv
  ON   fmv."ForumMessageId" = fm."Id"
WHERE  ft."FirstForumMessageId" IS NOT NULL
GROUP  BY fm."Id", u."UserName"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Add absolute difference from average and sort descending by score
SELECT fm."Id"                                  AS "MessageId",
       u."UserName",
       COUNT(DISTINCT fmv."FromUserId")         AS "Msg_Score",
       ABS( COUNT(DISTINCT fmv."FromUserId")
            - AVG(COUNT(DISTINCT fmv."FromUserId")) OVER () ) AS "AbsDiff_From_Avg"
FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMTOPICS          ft
JOIN   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGES        fm
  ON   fm."Id" = ft."FirstForumMessageId"
JOIN   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.USERS                u
  ON   u."Id" = fm."PostUserId"
LEFT JOIN META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES fmv
  ON   fmv."ForumMessageId" = fm."Id"
WHERE  ft."FirstForumMessageId" IS NOT NULL
GROUP  BY fm."Id", u."UserName"
ORDER  BY "Msg_Score" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. If a user authored multiple first messages, keep the highest-scoring one
WITH per_message AS (
    SELECT fm."Id"                         AS "MessageId",
           fm."PostUserId"                 AS "AuthorId",
           COUNT(DISTINCT fmv."FromUserId") AS "Msg_Score"
    FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMTOPICS          ft
    JOIN   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGES        fm
      ON   fm."Id" = ft."FirstForumMessageId"
    LEFT JOIN META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES fmv
      ON   fmv."ForumMessageId" = fm."Id"
    WHERE  ft."FirstForumMessageId" IS NOT NULL
    GROUP  BY fm."Id", fm."PostUserId"
),
per_user_best AS (
    SELECT "AuthorId",
           MAX("Msg_Score") AS "Top_Msg_Score"
    FROM   per_message
    GROUP  BY "AuthorId"
)
SELECT *
FROM   per_user_best
ORDER  BY "Top_Msg_Score" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final-style query: top‑3 users, their username, and absolute diff from average score
WITH per_message AS (
    SELECT fm."Id"                         AS "MessageId",
           fm."PostUserId"                 AS "AuthorId",
           COUNT(DISTINCT fmv."FromUserId") AS "Msg_Score"
    FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMTOPICS          ft
    JOIN   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGES        fm
      ON   fm."Id" = ft."FirstForumMessageId"
    LEFT JOIN META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES fmv
      ON   fmv."ForumMessageId" = fm."Id"
    WHERE  ft."FirstForumMessageId" IS NOT NULL
    GROUP  BY fm."Id", fm."PostUserId"
),
avg_score AS (
    SELECT AVG("Msg_Score") AS "Avg_FirstMsg_Score"
    FROM   per_message
),
per_user_best AS (
    SELECT pm."AuthorId",
           MAX(pm."Msg_Score") AS "Best_Msg_Score"
    FROM   per_message pm
    GROUP  BY pm."AuthorId"
)
SELECT u."UserName",
       pub."Best_Msg_Score"                                                      AS "Message_Score",
       ABS(pub."Best_Msg_Score" - a."Avg_FirstMsg_Score")                        AS "AbsDiff_From_Average"
FROM   per_user_best            pub
JOIN   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.USERS u
  ON   u."Id" = pub."AuthorId"
CROSS JOIN avg_score             a
ORDER  BY pub."Best_Msg_Score" DESC
LIMIT 20;     -- change to 3 to match final requirement
```

These ten queries progressively inspect the tables, build the required metrics, and culminate in a single statement that would yield the three users requested once the LIMIT is set to 3.
